{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "purpose": "The machine-readable, normative canonical AST contract. Each kind's ordinal is its wire number in every binding; scripts/tooling/generate-node-kinds.mjs generates every table that enumerates kinds from this file. C, Swift, Kotlin, and TypeScript declare projections of this shape, and scripts/audit/check-ast-projections.mjs checks the hand-written projections plus the prose and debug-dump tables against this file. Formula is the only kind whose placement mode varies; placement for Code, CodeBlock, Directive, DirectiveBlock, and FormulaBlock is implied by the kind.",
    "prose": "docs/specs/canonical-ast.md",
    "dumpGrammar": "docs/specs/canonical-ast-dump.md",
    "walk": {
        "visitor": "One exhaustive MarkupVisitor supplies typed visit(node, phase) callbacks for the explicit-stack walker. Only the walker dispatches nodes and schedules descendants. Callbacks accumulate results in visitor state and return no value: Void in Swift, Unit in Kotlin, undefined in TypeScript. No public single-node dispatch or result-returning visitor exists.",
        "phases": ["enter", "exit"],
        "order": "Depth first. Every Markup node enters, visits its owned Markup fields in canonical traversal order with arrays retaining stored order, then exits. Relations remain named fields, never projected into generic children. Document visits metadata when present, then content. Cite visits citations; Citation visits the Footnote of a footnote(note) referent, then prefix, then suffix. Referent labels are not traversed."
    },
    "enums": {
        "Placement": ["embedded", "standalone"],
        "BibMode": ["normal", "authorInText", "suppressAuthor"],
        "ListFlavor": ["bullet", "ordered"],
        "Flow": ["none", "left", "center", "right"]
    },
